From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] util/disk_cache: a put the cache already holds is dropped before compressing or evicting (RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN); zlib level (RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ZLIB_LEVEL)

Upstream compresses every put (zlib at level 9, Z_BEST_COMPRESSION: the PS5
build has no zstd) and then writes it. The multi-file cache first evicts (up to
8 times while over MESA_SHADER_CACHE_MAX_SIZE; each eviction reads a random
folder whole, two fstatat per file) and only after opening, locking and looking
for the final file finds that it is there. The database looks only in the part
it writes to, and only after making room, so a key held by another part is
stored a second time.

RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN=1 (exactly "1", read once per process):
- multi-file: one access() on the entry's file; if it is there, nothing else
  (no compression, no eviction, no file calls);
- database: before compressing, every part that exists is asked
  (mesa_cache_db_multipart_has_entry; no file access for the PS5's exclusively
  owned parts); a known key is dropped;
- database: the has-space look and the write become one step under the part's
  lock (mesa_cache_db_entry_write_ex with compact_if_full=false). Upstream,
  writers racing near a part's limit both pass mesa_cache_db_has_space, and
  the second then compacts the part, evicting half of it, oldest first: the
  entries this run just wrote. Now a full part is passed over for the next;
  compaction happens only when every part is full, as upstream;
- database, exclusive parts: a part found absent is remembered, so a lookup
  that misses no longer looks for every absent part's folder every time
  (mesa_cache_db_multipart_read_entry; up to 49 stat calls per miss).
Off: upstream behaviour, one cached flag read per put and per database miss.

RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ZLIB_LEVEL=<0..9> (one digit, read once per process;
anything else keeps level 9): the zlib level of util_compress_deflate, which
only the disk cache uses here. A lower level makes bigger entries and costs the
disk threads far less time; inflate reads any level, so entries written either
way mix in one cache.

One stderr line "<NAME>=<value> on" at first use of each. The database check is
on the key's first 64 bits, the same test mesa_cache_db_entry_write already
makes before it writes. Nothing about keys, entries, the file formats or the
cache UUID changes. Ours.

Compiled with the driver's flags, syntax only. Not linked, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5
---
diff --git a/src/util/compress.c b/src/util/compress.c
index 1f4b429..f754614 100644
--- a/src/util/compress.c
+++ b/src/util/compress.c
@@ -40,8 +40,12 @@
 
 #include "util/compress.h"
 #include "util/perf/cpu_trace.h"
+#include "util/u_atomic.h"
 #include "macros.h"
 
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+
 /* 3 is the recomended level, with 22 as the absolute maximum */
 #define ZSTD_COMPRESSION_LEVEL 3
 
@@ -96,7 +100,21 @@ util_compress_deflate(const uint8_t *in_data, size_t in_data_size,
    strm.avail_in = in_data_size;
    strm.avail_out = out_buff_size;
 
-   int ret = deflateInit(&strm, Z_BEST_COMPRESSION);
+   /* EglantinePS5: RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ZLIB_LEVEL=<0..9> (read once per process; anything else
+    * is upstream's Z_BEST_COMPRESSION, 9). The disk cache's threads compress every put before
+    * they write it, and level 9 is the slowest; a lower level only makes bigger entries. Any
+    * level reads back the same (inflate does not care), so caches written either way mix. */
+   static int level = -2;
+   int asked = p_atomic_read(&level);
+   if (asked == -2) {
+      const char *value = getenv("RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ZLIB_LEVEL");
+      asked = value && value[0] >= '0' && value[0] <= '9' && value[1] == '\0'
+                 ? value[0] - '0' : -1;
+      if (p_atomic_cmpxchg(&level, -2, asked) == -2 && asked >= 0)
+         fprintf(stderr, "RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ZLIB_LEVEL=%d on\n", asked);
+   }
+
+   int ret = deflateInit(&strm, asked >= 0 ? asked : Z_BEST_COMPRESSION);
    if (ret != Z_OK) {
        (void) deflateEnd(&strm);
        return 0;
diff --git a/src/util/disk_cache.c b/src/util/disk_cache.c
index 1f43388..54684a4 100644
--- a/src/util/disk_cache.c
+++ b/src/util/disk_cache.c
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <dirent.h>
